# Optional fallback for the End TimeKeeper pipe when it cannot call the TimeKeeper MCP tool.
# Copy beside the installed pipe.md as .env and use absolute paths.
# The pipe runs `. ./.env && eval "$TIMEKEEPER_END_COMMAND"` in bash:
# wrap the whole value in single quotes and use forward slashes, also on Windows.
# Windows example (Screenpipe's bundled bun runs the TypeScript file directly):
# TIMEKEEPER_END_COMMAND='"C:/Users/<you>/AppData/Local/screenpipe/bun.exe" "C:/path/to/TimeKeeper/src/mcp/end-session.ts"'
# macOS example:
# TIMEKEEPER_END_COMMAND='bun "/path/to/TimeKeeper/src/mcp/end-session.ts"'
TIMEKEEPER_END_COMMAND=

# The command calls the API at http://127.0.0.1:8787. Set TIMEKEEPER_API_URL as a user environment variable if needed.
